# Middle-half CPU pin

`nproc` cores, use the **middle half** (skip first and last quarter). On this
12-core machine that is `taskset -c 3-8`.

```bash
n=$(nproc)
start=$((n / 4))
end=$((start + n / 2 - 1))
taskset -c ${start}-${end}
```

Pin **cargo** and the **app binary** this way. Do not spread across all cores.
Agents: `taskset -c 3-8` on this 12-core box (same formula). Never `0-7` as a
habit — that is the first 8, not the middle half.
